// The application's icon, in the two places Windows looks for one.
//
// "1" is what Explorer, the file properties and the installer read off the executable: the shell
// takes the icon group with the lowest ordinal. "GLFW_ICON" is the name GLFW looks up by when it
// registers the window class, and is what puts the icon in the title bar, on the taskbar button
// and in the Alt-Tab list. Same file for both, so there is one icon and not two that drift.
//
// The file is generated from the mark's geometry rather than drawn by hand; see
// design/make-icon.ps1. It carries 16 through 256 pixels, the small sizes using the single-ring
// form of the mark, because three rings at sixteen pixels is three grey lines.
1 ICON "woodshed.ico"
GLFW_ICON ICON "woodshed.ico"
